e government. The artist initially declined the government's offer of exile in exchange for release, as he indicated in a l etter published by Hyperallergic ahead of his sentencing . However, Otero AlcÃ¡ntara eventually accepted exile while serving time, telling El PaÃ­s , â€œI never thought of leaving, but the regime has insinuated that thereâ€™s no option for me to walk through the streets of Cuba, because of the threat theyâ€™ve made me believe I am, or that people believe I am.â€ â€œI realize that the art I make represents a danger for them,â€ the artist continued during the 2024 interview with the Spanish newspaper. â€œThe options are between exile, or remaining [in Cuba] and always being in trouble.â€ Fusco pointed to two other prominent political prisoners, Felix Navarro and JosÃ© Daniel Ferrer, who were arrested in 2021 and paroled in 2025, only to be arrested again shortly thereafter, in her email correspondence with Hyperallergic . The artist's partner, curator Claudia Genlui Hidalgo, wrote that â€œAlcÃ¡ntara is treated differently from the rest of the prisonersâ€ in the foreword of an interview with the artist for Hyperallergic in 2023, reporting that he was routinely denied his right to personal phone calls and letters, and â€œsubjected to harassment and psychological torture.â€ Nevertheless, from myriad hunger strikes over the brutality in Guanajay and the detention of political prisoners, to honing in on drawing and participatory conceptual art , Otero AlcÃ¡ntara continued his activism and art practice while incarcerated. â€œI am very glad that Luis does not have to suffer the deprivations he lived with for five long years,â€ Fusco said, noting that the artist wants to enjoy his new life in the US and continue his art practice. However, she recognized â€œforced exile is just one more injustice committed against him.â€ Though Otero AlcÃ¡ntara is no longer incarcerated, other dissident artists, including Grammy-winning rapper and fellow SIM member Maykel â€œOsorboâ€ Castillo PÃ©rez, remain behind bars as political prisoners. PÃ©rez, whose song â€œPatria y Vidaâ€ (2021) became emblematic of the July 2021 protests, was arrested alongside Otero AlcÃ¡ntara and sentenced to nine years in 2022.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;SdiA_4fwQGm3nrNm5XDem5khlR4SrIphs99IrtCPn-4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx:Cuban Artist Luis Manuel Otero AlcÃ¡ntara Exiled to the USƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ZUC5iDvi5EmoRZbmxoWP-Pe5ncyxHv-SSN1vdhrOsEUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;iYqDasnuSbHIdJDL5D-FRd_jj6hPFRtT7IuWTHzS-sMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxThttps://hyperallergic.com/cuban-artist-luis-manuel-otero-alcantara-exiled-to-the-us/ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ITeolawe0yNSgBQ1EiIbJs7BwNHYdz0EU_45Or9Vb2sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx:cuban-artist-luis-manuel-otero-alca-ntara-exiled-to-the-usƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;YEtXiSr67iaRQtLWK2gT4rJ-2Pi-v8bD9qz6TaOMasoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwSyndicationSourceBundleƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;X844r5RBpD7x06jhwmzzyAeqIrHDHDm84azi_hrLARwƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkgcultureƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ludfxwORWxiIw7X0gpbUAfZFaWNHdUbK4HmTBwowewEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;QOM-WieAw2Ni4Ln33jyLTpaYo5XZ2P6L3jumnsjABEIƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-yMANK6sVQRt875yWrDmvr